# Copy to .env and edit. .env is git-ignored.
# Nothing here is needed by `checkpoint view` on loopback, which is the single-user
# local default. Two things change that: this stack and the cloud deploys bind
# 0.0.0.0, where CHECKPOINT_DASHBOARD_API_KEY is required and the dashboard exits
# rather than start without it; and judged [P] criteria need a provider key.
# Scenarios whose criteria are all assertions need neither.

# --- LLM provider keys (used by the judge / failure analyzer) ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Dashboard server ---
CHECKPOINT_PORT=4001
CHECKPOINT_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# CHECKPOINT_HOME=/data/config       # Set inside the container; override only for unusual paths

# --- Cloud / shared deployment hardening ---
# Required whenever the dashboard binds off loopback, which docker-compose.yml,
# fly.toml and render.yaml all do. Every /api/* write then requires
# `Authorization: Bearer <this value>`.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# CHECKPOINT_DASHBOARD_API_KEY=

# When set to 1, also require the bearer token on /api/* reads
# (dashboard SPA still works — it includes the token in fetches).
# CHECKPOINT_DASHBOARD_AUTH_READS=

# When set to 1, disable POST /api/jobs entirely. Use for a viewer-only
# instance that browses run history but can't spawn `checkpoint run`.
# CHECKPOINT_DASHBOARD_READ_ONLY=
